# Vercel only needs the Next.js app in frontend/ (built as a static export; see
# vercel.json). Everything below is the Python backend (deployed separately on
# Render) — without this file, Vercel's zero-config detection sees the
# top-level `api/` folder full of .py files plus requirements.txt at the
# root and auto-wraps api/main.py as a Python Serverless Function, bundling
# the *entire* requirements.txt (numpy/pandas/scikit-learn/spaCy/Airflow/
# Playwright...) into it — that's what blew past the 500MB function limit.
#
# Every pattern is anchored to the repository root with a leading "/": unanchored,
# "api/" and "research/" also matched frontend/lib/api/ and frontend/app/research/,
# so Vercel built the app without its API client.
/api/
/models/
/pipeline/
/research/
/docs/
/scripts/
/requirements.txt
/requirements-api.txt
/schema.sql
/schema_migration_002.sql
/schema_migration_003.sql
/seed_demo.sql
/.github/
/.venv/
/README.md
